import { pagePath } from '../../i18n';
---
  <p>The public pages of this website set no cookies, not even analytical ones. Only when you log in to the client account (/account/) do we set strictly necessary cookies: one that keeps you logged in (from Supabase) and one that remembers your language. They are needed to log in, so no consent is required, and we use them for nothing else.</p>

  <h2>Visitor statistics without cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Vercel Web Analytics to see how many people visit which pages. It works without cookies and without storing anything in your browser. It records the page, the site you came from, country, browser, operating system and device type. Your IP address is not stored, and you cannot be recognised on other sites or on a later day.</p>

  <h2>What we don't use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No Google Analytics, and no statistics that follow you across sites or over time</li>
    <li>No advertising pixels, such as those from Meta, LinkedIn or TikTok</li>
    <li>No embedded videos from YouTube or Vimeo; our videos are on our own server</li>
    <li>No fonts from Google Fonts; the typeface is on our own server too</li>
    <li>No storage in your browser, except your choice of light or dark mode if you change it, and that you closed the season message</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why you see no cookie banner</h2>
  <p>A cookie banner is needed when a site sets cookies or trackers that require consent. We don't, so there is nothing to accept or decline.</p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>If we ever add something that sets cookies, we will ask for your consent first, with a decline button just as clear as the accept button. We will update this page too.</p>

  <p>More about how we handle data is in the <a href={pagePath('en', 'privacy')}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
